  "verbalization": "The compound [(3S,5aS,6S,7S,9aS)-6-[2-[(5aS,6S,7R,9aS)-7-acetyloxy-2,2,5a,7-tetramethyl-3-oxo-4,5,6,8,9,9a-hexahydrobenzo[b]oxepin-6-yl]ethyl]-7-acetyloxy-2,2,5a,7-tetramethyl-4,5,6,8,9,9a-hexahydro-3H-benzo[b]oxepin-3-yl] acetate) is associated with U251 through multiple pathways. It is a target of several compounds, including (1R,3R,4S,7S,9S,11S,13R,14R,15R)-4,11,13,14-tetrahydroxy-7-[(2Z,4R)-4-(hydroxymethyl)hex-2-en-2-yl]-3,9,15-trimethoxy-12,12-dimethyl-6,17-dioxabicyclo[11.3.1]heptadecan-5-one, Dendridine A, and Certonardosterol E3. These compounds are known to interact with U251, a glioblastoma cell line, suggesting that the compound may exert its effects through these pathways. The evidence suggests that the compound may act as a modulator of U251, potentially through interactions with the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14 or microtubule-associated proteins. The relationship is supported by multiple independent targets, indicating a plausible mechanism of action. The strength of the evidence is moderate, with some variability in the scores, but the consistent association across different targets supports a potential role in U251 regulation.",
